  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I am a software engineer with more than thirteen years of practice. Most of that time went into C++ services on Linux, especially game servers: network entry, login, game logic, and the platform layer beside them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The work has also been done in Go, Python, Lua, and TypeScript. The language followed the service boundary. A gateway, a game process, and a platform API do not have to share one runtime.
  </p>
  <h2>What I work on</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Backend architecture and the split between gateway, login, and game services</li>
    <li>Distributed systems: who owns session state, and what may be retried</li>
    <li>C++ and Linux systems programming</li>
    <li>Real-time communication, where a dropped peer has to be an explicit state</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What I am studying</h2>
  <p>
    AI systems, real-time voice, intelligent hardware, edge computing, and ROS 2. These are current practice. I do not describe them as a long production record.
  </p>
  <p>
    Public writing and project notes are on this site. Private repositories stay off this page.
  </p>
</Base>
